WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.157
This script begins a transaction.

00:00:02.157 --> 00:00:07.482
It lowercases and trims emails only when the stored value is actually different.

00:00:07.482 --> 00:00:10.217
RETURNING shows which rows changed.

00:00:10.217 --> 00:00:12.822
Then ROLLBACK discards the changes.

00:00:12.822 --> 00:00:19.407
This is a useful teaching pattern because you can inspect the effect without permanently modifying the source

00:00:19.407 --> 00:00:24.922
table. Once a quality rule is well understood, prevention may be better than repeated cleanup.

00:00:24.922 --> 00:00:28.807
Constraints can stop known invalid values at write time.

00:00:28.807 --> 00:00:34.422
When updates are required, preview the target rows, change only what is justified,

00:00:34.422 --> 00:00:38.560
and use RETURNING or an audit log so the transformation can be reviewed.
